Job Req Number: 115298

Time Type: Full Time

Move forward as Quality specialist at DSV in Moerdijk

You are driven by quality, compliance and continuous improvement. As a quality specialist at DSV Contract Logistics, you are responsible for managing and improving the Quality Management System (QMS) across the organization and specially for one of our high value clients.

You get it done

You lead quality management initiatives, support site management and ensure compliance with customer, legal and third party requirements.

How you do this? You combine governance with practical application, ensuring quality standards are understood and applied in daily operations .You achieve this by:


planning, implementing and maintaining the Quality Management System (QMS);
ensuring quality governance and compliance across sites;
promoting a strong quality culture within the organization;
coordinating internal and external audits and follow up actions;
monitoring customer, regulatory and third party requirements.


Your team stands out within DSV as a group of experienced and driven colleagues, all sharing a passion for the profession and working together on DSV’s strategy.

We are DSV, we grow

DSV is a global provider of transport and logistics services. With offices in more than 90 countries and a growing network of partners, there is no place in the world we cannot reach via transport by air, sea, rail, courier or road or where we can offer storage in warehouses.

“Quality is embedded in the way we work. As a CL Quality specialist, you ensure that standards are not just defined, but truly lived throughout the operation.”; 

says Philip Verweij, Site Manager.

In the Netherlands, we operate from over 40 branches, with more than 5,000 colleagues. Together we rise to the challenge of a rapidly changing environment. We make quick decisions at every level and combine ambition and teamwork. This is how we move forward and make a difference together.

You bring


proven experience in quality management within a logistics or operational environment;
knowledge of Quality Management Systems and audit methodologies;
experience with compliance and continuous improvement;
strong analytical and communication skills;
a proactive and structured mindset;
good command of the English language.


It all counts for this vacancy of quality specialist in Moerdijk. A full time role with clear impact on quality and compliance, development opportunities and a professional international working environment.

You get

Working at DSV means working at one of the top players in the logistics market. DSV is entrepreneurial and competitive, which is why we always want to grow as an organization. That is why we are looking for people who want to grow with us. Besides a challenging job in an international environment we also offer:


a salary indication between € 3.500,- & € 4.000,-, based on your knowledge and experience;
28 days of annual leave and 8% holiday allowance;
ample opportunities for personal and professional development;
the space and freedom to take initiative in an informal working environment;
and, of course, a great team to work with.


Move forward

Send your resume with motivation or leave your details and we will contact you. Any questions about this vacancy? Our corporate recruiter a.i. Rolf Buitenkamp answers all your questions via +31 (0)6 1421 5279 or ext.rolf.buitenkamp@dsv.com.

We will only contact you via our official company email addresses (e.g., @dsv.com or @nl.dsv.com) and never reach out to candidates through personal email providers such as Gmail or Hotmail.

DSV – Global transport and logistics

Working at DSV means playing in a different league.

As a global leader in transport and logistics, we have been on an extraordinary journey of growth. Let’s grow together as we continue to innovate, digitalise and build on our achievements.

With close to 150,000 colleagues in over 90 countries, we work every day to offer solid services and meet our customers’ needs and help them achieve their goals. We know that the best way to achieve this is by bringing in new talent, fresh perspectives and ambitious individuals like you.

At DSV, performance is in our DNA. We don’t just work – we aim to shape the future of logistics. This ambition fuels a dynamic environment built on collaboration with world-class team players, accountability and action. We value inclusivity, embrace different cultures and respect the dignity and rights of every individual. If you want to make an impact, be trusted by customers and grow your career in a forward-thinking company – this is the place to be.

Start here. Go anywhere

Visit dsv.com and follow us on LinkedIn and Facebook. 
